# STIG RHEL-09-411085: GNOME login-banner-enable
# STIG ID: V-258056 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `r9-rhel-09-411085-dconf-login-banner-enable-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG RHEL-09-411085: RHEL 9 must automatically lock an account when three unsuccessful logon attempts`
    description `RHEL 9 must automatically lock an account when three unsuccessful logon attempts occur during a 15-minute time period.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `rhel9,stig,disa-stig,gnome,dconf`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:RHEL-09-411085,NIST-800-53:AC-7`
    control_objective `AC-7`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:os-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for RHEL-09-411085.`

    component_id `comp-r9-os`

    impl_AC_7 `This control is validated by checking the required system configuration against the DISA STIG baseline for RHEL 9.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT dconf_check
        schema `org.gnome.login-screen`
        key `banner-message-enable`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE setting_correct
        applicable boolean = true
        value string = `true`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN dconf_setting
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF setting_correct
            OBJECT_REF dconf_check
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
